# Keep LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Windows checkouts convert LF -> CRLF by default, which makes `gofmt -l` report every .go
# file as unformatted (CRLF is not gofmt's output) and fails the `make check` fmt gate on the
# windows/amd64 CI row. Pinning eol=lf keeps one canonical form everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The vendored native libs are binary and must never be eol-converted. The C header is NOT
# excluded — it is text, and normalising it to LF is what we want: it matches what
# vendor_release.sh writes, so the Windows runner's CRLF copy cannot churn the committed file.
*.a binary
*.zip binary
